 "poem": "West Wind, bring to us a delicate sensation,\nSmell it round our lips; do not provocation\nWeary your ministrations with provocation,\nDimmer and dimmer nightingales can\nSoftly sing in the myrtle-wood's tree,\nBrighter their song than the morning misty,\nMaking our spirits sensation.\nBreathe on our blood again,\nBreath over it once more: it is although\nHeart-sick as last night, though its sorrow\nStill may gush from it at celebration,\nBut already through everyone",
